// 4 Brothers World V2 — part 23: a bigger, more beautiful Fuzzy World.
//  * The slinger tribes wear their first, softer fur patterns again (stored pixel for pixel).
//  * Ridgebacks and shellbacks are the cavalry's own animals, tame like horses: they graze and wander, and only fight
//    if you hit them. Shellbacks are now far bigger than ridgebacks.
//  * Fuzzy World is 400 blocks wider. East of Gnarlroot's Hollow lies the Deep Tanglewood, a jungle of giant trees,
//    then a cliff with a waterfall up to the Woolly Highlands, flat grassland where herds of Curlmanes charge.
//    Players' building is kept: block changes are stored under their old numbers, so nothing moves.
//  * Giant jungle trees with real bark, ferns, flowers, climbable lianas, glowcaps; fireflies at dusk and night,
//    sun shafts, pollen and butterflies by day, and far-off giant trees behind the jungle.
//  * Tanglehold's families live in home-trees, like the brothers' drawing: woven nest pods up in the branches,
//    a fenced ring deck round the trunk, and a log swing.
//  * Scorpion dens (a rock mound full of burrows and winding tunnels) in the Sunbake Desert and the Deep Tanglewood,
//    each with a Mother Scorpion (three tails, a back of spikes) guarding her hoard, and treasure along the tunnels.
